GC-Chiptune
===========

The code in this repository AND the built `.dol` are under the MIT licence
(below).

The TimGM6mb soundfont, distributed **alongside** the binary in the release,
remains under **GPL-2.0**. They are two separate works on the same medium: the
player reads a data file at start-up, it does not derive from it. Each therefore
keeps its own licence.

That was not true for a while: the soundfont was **embedded in the `.dol`**,
which made it a single work and imposed GPL-2.0 on the whole binary. It was
taken back out — for memory first (5.7 MB permanently out of the console's 24,
see docs/STATUS.md §12.20), and the licence followed.

Redistributing the soundfont requires providing its source: that is the purpose
of `soundfont-source-TimGM6mb.sf2` in the release, and of
`extern/soundfont/TimGM6mb.sf2` here — the only file in `extern/` that is
versioned, and for exactly that reason.

Replacing TimGM6mb with MuseScore's `MS Basic` (MIT) would make the release
entirely permissive, binary and data.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

  libogc2, libfat                        see their repositories
  libxmp                                 LGPL-2.1-or-later
  TinySoundFont, TinyMidiLoader          MIT
  GRRLIB                                 MIT
  FreeType                               FTL or GPL-2-or-later
  libpng, zlib, brotli, bzip2            permissive
  DejaVu Sans Condensed (embedded)       Bitstream Vera + Arev, permissive
  TimGM6mb.sf2 (Tim Brechbill)           GPL-2.0, separate file

On TimGM6mb: its author states that he created some of the samples himself, the
others being "either in the public domain or under the GPL". That provenance
remains a declaration.


